```
Reason:
The code assumes that the MCP251x CAN controller will enter configuration mode within a fixed time frame after a reset, specifically after a 5ms delay. If the device takes longer to stabilize, the check for the configuration mode will fail, leading to an error being returned prematurely.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
timeout = jiffies + HZ;
while ((mcp251x_read_reg(spi, CANSTAT) & CANCTRL_REQOP_MASK) !=
       CANCTRL_REQOP_CONF) {
    usleep_range(MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000,
                 MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000 * 2);
    if (time_after(jiffies, timeout)) {
        dev_err(&spi->dev,
            "MCP251x didn't enter in conf mode after reset\n");
        return -EBUSY;
    }
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a loop that continuously checks if the MCP251x has entered configuration mode, allowing for retries and a longer wait time. This accounts for variability in power-up times across different boards, ensuring that the device has sufficient time to stabilize before checking its state. If the device does not enter the expected state within the timeout period, an error is logged, and the function returns an appropriate error code.

